UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"Mecklenburg-Vorpommern''s fisheries authority states that angling in its coastal waters (the Bodden, Haffe, Peenestrom, Achterwasser and the Baltic Sea within German territorial waters) always needs three personal documents: a Fischereischein, an Angelerlaubnis and proof of payment of the state fishing fee. There are no free angling waters in MV. Visitors can obtain a temporary Touristenfischereischein valid for up to 28 days. Check the LALLF M-V for how to obtain each document before you travel.","sourceUrl":"https://www.lallf.de/fischerei/angelfischerei/fischereidokumente-allg/"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["Baltic coastal fishing in Mecklenburg-Vorpommern requires a Fischereischein, an Angelerlaubnis (coastal fishing permit) and proof of payment of the state Fischereiabgabe","Sea trout have a minimum size and a closed season for coloured fish","Cod bag limits are set annually by EU rules — check before keeping fish"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'ruegen-baltic-sea-trout';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"The Schleswig-Holstein Wadden Sea National Park authority states that angling in the coastal strip is generally possible, except in breeding and resting sites in salt marshes that are marked on site. Angling from boats is possible almost everywhere in the park, but is prohibited in the usage-free zone south of the Hindenburgdamm. Check the national-park rules and signage before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.nationalpark-wattenmeer.de/wissensbeitrag/sport-und-freizeitfischerei/"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'sylt-north-sea';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"boat":true,"notes":"Recreational bluefin tuna fishing in the Mediterranean from a French-flagged or EU-registered recreational or charter vessel requires an annual authorisation from the regional maritime authority (DIRM), applied for with the CERFA form published by the Ministry of the Sea. Vessels flying the flag of a non-EU state may not fish bluefin tuna recreationally. A tuna that is retained must be tagged immediately with the marking ring supplied, and each landing must be declared to FranceAgriMer within 48 hours. Check the Ministry of the Sea and current French and ICCAT rules before targeting tuna.","sourceUrl":"https://www.mer.gouv.fr/pratiquer-la-peche-de-loisir-au-thon-rouge"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'sete-mediterranean-tuna';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"The Ministry of the Sea advises shore anglers to respect minimum sizes and closed seasons, to leave no waste on the foreshore and to tell someone where they are going before setting out. Recreational fishers aged 16 and over who target designated sensitive species, including sea bass in the Channel and Bay of Biscay zones, must register each year through the RecFishing app and declare catches daily. Catches are marked by removing the lower part of the tail fin. Check the Ministry''s shellfish sanitary zone maps before gathering shellfish, and check tide times carefully before fishing rock marks.","sourceUrl":"https://www.mer.gouv.fr/peche-de-loisir-en-mer"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["No licence required for recreational sea fishing","Recreational anglers aged 16 and over targeting sea bass in the Channel must register annually through the RecFishing app and declare their catches; catches must be marked by removing the lower part of the tail fin — check the Ministry of the Sea before fishing","Bass minimum size and bag limits apply","Tides here are among the largest in Europe — check times carefully before fishing rock marks"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'normandy-bass-cotentin';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"boat":true,"notes":"The Egadi Islands Marine Protected Area is zoned: A (integral reserve, western Marettimo and the Maraone islet), B (general reserve around the Faraglione of Favignana, west Levanzo and parts of Marettimo), C (partial reserve: all of Favignana, and the east sides of Levanzo and Marettimo) and D (the protection zone between the islands). The MPA lists sport fishing for zones B and C only, under authorisation from the MPA management body, and spearfishing is prohibited throughout the MPA. Check the MPA''s current zoning map and authorisation procedure before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.ampisoleegadi.it/index.php/zonazione/"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'sicily-bluefin-tuna';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"boat":true,"notes":"The Canary Islands government issues recreational sea-fishing licences in three classes: class 1 for surface trolling from a vessel, class 2 for spearfishing and class 3 for surface fishing from land or from a vessel without trolling. Licences are valid for three years and are applied for through the regional electronic office. Marlins, tunas, swordfish and hake are species under differentiated protection that need a separate authorisation from Spain''s national fisheries ministry. Check the Canary Islands government and the ministry for current rules before targeting them.","sourceUrl":"https://www.gobiernodecanarias.org/pesca/temas/pesca_recreativa/licencias.html"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'canary-islands-marlin';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"If fishing inside the Cap de Creus Natural Park (Girona coast), the park authority requires a special park permit, obtained after environmental and fishing training, in addition to the general recreational fishing licence; permit holders must report catches daily and mark fish caught. Only catch-and-release fishing is allowed in the coves of Murtra, Caials and Tamariua, and fishing is banned in the S''Encalladora Integral Natural Reserve. Check the park''s current zoning and rules before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://parcsnaturals.gencat.cat/ca/xarxa-de-parcs/cap-creus/gaudeix-del-parc/guia-de-visita/que-shi-pot-fer/activitats-a-mar"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["Catalonia recreational sea fishing licence required","Catch reporting via the PescaREC app applies since March 2026","Some marine reserves along this coast are no-take and Cap de Creus Natural Park has its own fishing permit and zoning — check local zoning"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'costa-brava-spinning';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"HEALTH ADVICE: Mattilsynet (the Norwegian Food Safety Authority) publishes dietary advice for the Hardangerfjord/Sorfjorden area, which is contaminated with cadmium, lead, mercury, dioxins and PCB. The advice includes avoiding brosme and pollock in specified zones, pregnant and nursing women avoiding crab, lobster and stationary fish in the inner areas, and shellfish restrictions in designated zones. Read Mattilsynet''s current advice and zone descriptions before eating any catch, and confirm current Norwegian fishing rules.","sourceUrl":"https://www.mattilsynet.no/mat-og-drikke/forbrukere/unnga-fisk-og-skalldyr-fra-forurensede-havner-fjorder-og-innsjoer"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'hardangerfjord-sea-trout';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"HEALTH ADVICE: Mattilsynet (the Norwegian Food Safety Authority) publishes dietary advice for fish and shellfish from polluted fjords. For the inner Oslofjord (inside Drobak) it advises pregnant and nursing women and children under 5 not to eat cod fillet because of mercury, and advises the general population to avoid mussels from the inner harbour area because of PAH. Check Mattilsynet''s current advice for any fish you plan to eat, and confirm current Norwegian fishing rules.","sourceUrl":"https://www.mattilsynet.no/mat-og-drikke/forbrukere/unnga-fisk-og-skalldyr-fra-forurensede-havner-fjorder-og-innsjoer"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'oslofjord-sea-trout';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"boat":true,"notes":"HEALTH ADVICE: the Swedish Food Agency (Livsmedelsverket) warns that wild-caught char from Lake Vattern, and wild trout, whitefish and salmon from Vattern, can contain high levels of dioxin and PCB. Children, young people and anyone who is pregnant, breastfeeding or planning a pregnancy should eat these fish at most two to three times a year; other adults can eat them about once a week. The Agency also advises not eating eel at all. Check the Food Agency''s current advice before eating your catch, and confirm current fishing rules with the county board.","sourceUrl":"https://www.livsmedelsverket.se/matvanor-halsa--miljo/kostrad/fisk-som-kan-innehalla-miljogifter/"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'vattern-char';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"Lansstyrelsen Vastra Gotaland states that fishing with hand-held gear in the sea is free, but from 1 January to 31 March fishing for cod is prohibited inside the trawl boundary, fishing for cod is prohibited all year in the Gullmarsfjorden protection area, and from 1 October to 31 March fishing is prohibited in all protected areas (fredningsomraden). The county board''s Svenska Fiskeregler map service shows the protected areas. Check the current rules before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.lansstyrelsen.se/vastra-gotaland/djur/fiske.html"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["Rod fishing in Swedish saltwater is free and unlicensed","Cod: fishing for cod is prohibited inside the trawl boundary from 1 January to 31 March and all year in the Gullmarsfjorden protection area — check current limits before keeping any","All protected areas (fredningsomraden) are closed to fishing from 1 October to 31 March — check Svenska Fiskeregler for the map","Sea trout have minimum sizes and closed seasons near river mouths"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'bohuslan-coast-mackerel';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"notes":"Lansstyrelsen Vasterbotten manages the Vindelalven between Mankeforsen and Sarngejukkes as a quota water: permits are allocated by lottery, applications are open from 1 January to 30 April, results are announced from the second half of May, and you can apply for up to five fishing days. Fly fishing with a fly rod only applies on most quota waters, catch reporting is mandatory, and the season on the Vindelalven runs from 1 July to 20 August. Children under 16 go free with a guardian. Check the county board page for the current application rules.","sourceUrl":"https://www.lansstyrelsen.se/vasterbotten/djur/fiske/fiska-i-fjallen/ansok-om-fiske-i-kvoterade-vatten.html"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["The Vindelalven between Mankeforsen and Sarngejukkes is quota-managed: a lottery permit from Lansstyrelsen Vasterbotten is required (applications 1 January to 30 April), not an ordinary fiskekort","Fly fishing with a fly rod only on most quota waters; catch reporting is mandatory","The season is short (1 July to 20 August on the Vindelalven) — check the county board for current rules and salmon regulations"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'vindelalven-grayling';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"Lansstyrelsen Gotland (the county administrative board) states that fishing with hand-held tackle is free along the sea coast, but permission is needed in streams and most other inland waters. Sea trout are protected from 1 September to 31 January in 25 protected areas at 34 streams, and from 2025 the protection also applies within the watercourses, not just the mouths. Pike and perch are protected in the coastal waters out to four nautical miles around the whole of Gotland from 1 March to 31 May. Check the county board''s current rules and protected-area maps before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.lansstyrelsen.se/gotland/djur/fiske.html"}'::jsonb, regulations = '["Rod fishing in saltwater is free and needs no licence","Sea trout minimum size applies and coloured fish must be released","Sea trout are protected from 1 September to 31 January in protected areas at Gotland streams, including within the watercourses themselves — check the county board map","Pike and perch are protected in Gotland coastal waters (out to 4 nautical miles) from 1 March to 31 May"]'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'gotland-sea-trout';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"boat":true,"notes":"Metsahallitus issues the angling permit for the state waters of Lake Inarijarvi and Lake Nitsijarvi through its Eraluvat permit service. The permit is specific to the boating party, so one valid permit covers one boat, and the number of permits is limited. The state fisheries management fee also applies to lure anglers aged 18 to 69, while hook-and-line and ice fishing with one rod are free. The lake has more than 3,000 islands and many shallow areas. Check the Inari fisheries area rules and the permit terms before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.eraluvat.fi/en/areas/1504-inarijarvi-1185/products"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'inari-lake-trout';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"notes":"At Langinkoski (the lowest rapids of the Langinkoski branch of the Kymijoki, inside the Langinkoski nature reserve near Kotka city centre) Metsahallitus allows fly fishing only with an angling permit, and no more than eight people may fish at once. Native fish with an intact adipose fin may not be kept, to protect the salmon and sea trout runs. The season runs from 1 January to 30 September and from 1 December to 31 December. The state fisheries management fee also applies to anglers aged 18 to 69. Check the permit terms on Eraluvat, and other Kymijoki sections have different rules.","sourceUrl":"https://www.eraluvat.fi/en/fishing/fishing-permits/angling-permit/alueet/langinkoski.html"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'kymijoki-river';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"notes":"Metsahallitus manages fishing in the Ruunaa rapids as permit area 7525, running from Paasikoski to below Siikakoski and including Murroojarvi and Kattilajarvi. A rod-fishing permit and the state fisheries management fee are required for most anglers. Wading is prohibited from 1 September to 31 May, and fishing is banned in the Paasikoski to Mutikaisenkari section from 1 September to 30 November. Angling and jigging are not allowed in flowing water but are allowed in still water with a permit. Kattilakoski is a reserved rapid booked for groups. Check the permit terms on Eraluvat for current rules.","sourceUrl":"https://www.eraluvat.fi/kohteet/7525-ruunaan-kosket-527"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'ruunaa-rapids';

UPDATE public.spots SET access = '{"shore":true,"boat":true,"notes":"The City of Imatra divides the Vuoksi fishing waters into the Vuoksi itself (excluding Mellonlahti) and Mellonlahti, each with its own permit. On the Vuoksi, fly fishing, spinning and trolling are allowed, bait fishing and ice fishing need no Vuoksi permit, and motor trolling is limited to the stretch between Kyyronkoski and the border zone. All fishing is prohibited from 15 October to 15 November between the railway bridge and the river mouth, and grayling are protected from 1 April to 31 May. Check the City of Imatra''s current permit terms before fishing.","sourceUrl":"https://www.imatra.fi/asuminen-ja-ymparisto/virkistysalueet/kalastus/vuoksen-kalastusalueet-ja-lupaehdot"}'::jsonb, updated_at = now() WHERE slug = 'vuoksi-river-trout';

